variables.detailed:
Note[1]: 'length' is set to (sizeof(A) - 1) in DNS_NAME_INITNONABSOLUTE and sizeof(A) in DNS_NAME_INITABSOLUTE to allow C strings to be used to initialize 'ndata'.
Note[2]: The final value of offsets for DNS_NAME_INITABSOLUTE should match (sizeof(A) - 1) which is the offset of the root label.
Typical usage: unsigned char data[] = "\005value"; unsigned char offsets[] = { 0 }; dns_name_t value = DNS_NAME_INITNONABSOLUTE(data, offsets);
unsigned char data[] = "\005value"; unsigned char offsets[] = { 0, 6 }; dns_name_t value = DNS_NAME_INITABSOLUTE(data, offsets);

